Our results significantly reduce the dependence on d in DDPM convergence analyses. Given that the ambient dimension d often scales as 104 − 106 in common image/video tasks, this improvement is
substantial. Compared with the Oe(Le2√d/T ) rate for DDIM, our result shares the same d dependence while improving the dependence on the Lipschitz parameter L. We further established matching lower bounds, implying that our TV and KL rates are tight (up to logarithmic factors).
